{#
  T-4.23 — the shoppable video carousel.

  | Variable                      | Type    | Description                       |
  |-------------------------------|---------|-----------------------------------|
  | component.items[].embed_url   | string  | YouTube, TikTok, Instagram or a direct video file |
  | component.items[].poster      | ?string | Who posted it                     |
  | component.items[].product     | ?list   | Product picker; resolved at runtime |
  | component.items[].product_id  | ?string | Typed id, read when no product picked |
  | position                      | int     | Sorting number, from zero         |

  THE CARRIER IS T-4.21'S. `salla-slider type="carousel" centered` already draws
  a centred slide with its neighbours partly visible, and the progress-bar
  pagination is the same `slider-config` merge — so this section adds no third
  slider and no third indicator.

  THE VIDEO PLAYS IN THE PAGE, WITH NO COVER — the owner's ruling of 2026-10-12,
  which replaces the façade this section shipped with (a merchant cover image
  plus a play button, the embed created only on press). The owner found the
  cover a needless step and the new-tab fallback for unrecognised links wrong
  for a simple video. `partials/video-carousel.js` now mounts each player when
  its slide comes near the screen — an iframe for YouTube, TikTok and
  Instagram, a native <video> for a direct file — so the page still does not
  load every video up front, but a visitor's player does reach the platform
  without a press. Recorded in /docs/DERIVED-DECISIONS.md.

  THE PRODUCT LINE IS RESOLVED FROM ITS ID, exactly as the hotspot pill is, and
  through the same `partials/product-runtime` helpers. A renamed or repriced
  product needs no edit here.
#}
{% set video_items = component.items|default([]) %}

{% if video_items|length %}
    <section data-testid="store-home-video-carousel" class="s-block video-carousel container{{ video_items|length == 1 ? ' video-carousel--single' : '' }}">
        <div class="s-block__panel">
            <salla-slider
                type="carousel"
                class="video-carousel__slider"
                centered
                pagination
                slider-config='{"pagination":{"el":"#video-{{ position }}-slider .swiper-pagination","type":"progressbar","clickable":false}}'
                id="video-{{ position }}-slider">
                <div slot="items">
                    {% for item in video_items %}
                        {# The picker sends a list even with one choice, of products or of
                           ids; a typed product_id from before the picker is the fallback.
                           Same resolution as components/ui/hotspot-image.twig. #}
                        {% set video_product = item.product is defined and item.product ? item.product : null %}
                        {% if video_product is iterable %}
                            {% set video_product = video_product|first %}
                        {% endif %}
                        {% if video_product %}
                            {% set video_product_id = video_product.id is defined ? video_product.id : video_product %}
                        {% else %}
                            {% set video_product_id = item.product_id|default('') %}
                        {% endif %}
                        <div class="swiper-slide video-carousel__slide">
                            <div class="video-carousel__frame"
                                 data-video-slide
                                 data-embed-url="{{ item.embed_url }}"
                                 data-video-title="{{ item.poster
                                     ? trans('theme.video.frame_title_named', { name: item.poster })
                                     : trans('theme.video.frame_title') }}">

                                {% if item.poster %}
                                    {# The artboard bakes the poster's identity into the
                                       screenshot. A merchant's own still will not have
                                       it, so it is rendered — as text, never as a
                                       scraped avatar. #}
                                    <p class="video-carousel__poster"><bdi>{{ item.poster }}</bdi></p>
                                {% endif %}
                            </div>

                            {# Filled by partials/video-carousel.js from the product id,
                               and hidden until then so a failed lookup leaves no empty
                               row behind. Same contract as the hotspot pill. #}
                            {% if video_product_id %}
                                <div class="video-carousel__product"
                                     data-video-product
                                     data-product-id="{{ video_product_id }}"
                                     hidden></div>
                            {% endif %}
                        </div>
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
            </salla-slider>
        </div>
    </section>
{% endif %}
